{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And when he goes out, and he shall not die.</b> It appears that if he did not have the bells that produce the sound, he would be liable to death at the hands of Heaven. For if this were not so, and the intent were only regarding lacking garments, He should have said ״וְלֹא יָמוּת״ after the completion of the garments, or at the very least after the completion of the four garments of the High Priest, and not in the middle. Rather, it comes to teach about the specific detail — that he is liable even on account of the bells. And in the verse stated at the end of the making of the garments, where it is written ״וְהָיוּ עַל אַהֲרֹן וְגוֹ׳ וְלֹא יִשְׂאוּ עָוֹן וָמֵתוּ״ (Exodus 28:43), there it imposes liability upon one who serves lacking garments."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:14.666695355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}